# GEC Design Language

Follow patterns from About Us, home sections, and ganvex-mat — not generic SaaS marketing UI.

## Brand tokens (`globals.css` `@theme`)

- Primary: `mainColor` `#441752`, `secondaryColor`, `thirdColor`
- Accents: `otherColor` / `otherColorDark`, `other1`, `other2`
- Neutrals: `darkColor`, `lightColor`, `secondaryDark`, `secondaryLight`
- Radius: `rounded-main` (20px), `rounded-secondary`, `rounded-third`
- Purple brand is **intentional** — do not “de-purple” the site

## Layout utilities

```
.margin  → mx-4 md:mx-10
.spacing → py-10 md:py-20
```

Section pages usually combine `margin` + `spacing`, or bg band + inner `margin`.

## Surfaces & chrome

- Soft panels: `bg-lightColor dark:bg-darkColor` (often `/50`–`/60`)
- Inverted bands: `bg-darkColor dark:bg-lightColor` with careful text contrast
- Section labels: `Title` from `src/components/title-text.jsx` (uppercase, tracking)
- Banners: split title / description like `ReusableBanner` / About Us — image strip + content band below when matching that pattern
- Prefer `components/<feature>/*-section.jsx` composition for multi-section pages

## Do / Don’t

```jsx
// ✅ GEC — token surfaces, Title chrome, brand CTA
<section className="margin spacing">
  <Title>About Us</Title>
  <div className="bg-lightColor dark:bg-darkColor rounded-main p-4">…</div>
</section>

// ❌ Generic — purple gradient CTA blob, full-bleed text-on-hero overlay stack
<div className="bg-gradient-to-br from-violet-600 to-indigo-500 …">
```

## Accessibility (required)

- Sufficient contrast in **light and dark**
- Meaningful `alt` on `next/image`; decorative images: empty `alt` only when intentional
- Interactive controls: visible focus, keyboard operable, `aria-label` when label is visual-only
- Keep `lang` aligned with dominant copy on the page/section when adding markup
- Prefer shadcn primitives (button, dialog, sheet) for focus/ARIA behavior over custom widgets
